   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`delete INDEX` is implemented. All 5 tests pass, and `tools/check.py` exits 0 (tests plus the 100-character line-length rule).\n\n**Red:** before any implementation, the 3 new tests failed. The two store tests raised `AttributeError: module 'fieldnotes.store' has no attribute 'delete'`. The CLI test failed with `2 != 0`, because the CLI rejected `delete` as unknown.\n\n**Green:**\n- **`fieldnotes/store.py`:** new `delete(index)` removes and returns the note at that 1-based position. It raises `IndexError` for an out-of-range index and leaves the stored notes untouched in that case.\n- **`fieldnotes/cli.py`:** `delete INDEX` prints `deleted: <text>` and exits 0. A non-integer index, an out-of-range index, or a missing argument prints an error to stderr and exits 2. I also updated the usage strings and the docstring.\n- **Tests:** two store tests in `tests/test_store.py`, and a new `tests/test_cli.py` with two CLI tests. They cover successful deletion, out-of-range indexes (0, -1, too large), a non-numeric index and a missing argument.\n\n**Decision for you:** I chose 1-based indexes, but `list` doesn't currently print numbers, so users can't see which index to pass. I left `list` alone to avoid changing its output. Numbering it (`1  <created>  <text>`) would be a small follow-up if you want it.\n\nI ran the check against a temporary `NOTES_HOME` directory and deleted it afterwards, so no real notes were touched.",
