   "reply": "I added a `count` command that prints the number of notes. The project checks pass: all 6 tests ran OK and the line-length rule found nothing.\n\n- **Command:** `fieldnotes/cli.py` now handles `count` and prints `len(store.load())`. With no notes it prints `0`.\n- **Test:** `CountCommandTests` in `tests/test_cli.py` checks the output is `0` for an empty store and `2` after adding two notes.\n- **Refactor:** I moved the shared setup and `run_cli` helper from `DeleteCommandTests` into a `CliTestCase` base class, so the delete tests don't run twice.\n- **Checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set, so I ran it with a fresh temp directory.\n\nI didn't update the usage message in `cli.py` or the module docstring, so neither mentions `count`.",
